---
import Container from "../components/Container.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import SectionHeader from "../components/SectionHeader.astro";
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout title="Terms — Conclave AX" description="Terms for using Conclave AX, connected Workspaces, AI Workers, Accounts, and the public website.">
  <Section>
    <Container>
      <SectionHeader eyebrow="Terms" title="Terms of Service" description="General terms governing access to Conclave AX, connected execution environments, third-party AI providers, and the public website." headingLevel={1} />
      <div class="legal-content">
        <h2>1. Service overview</h2>
        <p>Conclave AX provides software for coordinating people, AI models, tools, execution environments, workflows, and verification around Projects and Workstreams.</p>

        <h2>2. Your account and Project activity</h2>
        <p>You are responsible for protecting your authentication credentials and for actions taken through authorized sessions. Project owners and collaborators are responsible for granting appropriate access to Project content and execution capabilities.</p>

        <h2>3. Connected Workspaces</h2>
        <p>When you connect a machine as a Workspace, you authorize Conclave AX to dispatch work that is permitted by the Workspace's active Project grants and local execution policy. Workspace owners remain responsible for the machine, local repositories, installed software, and revoking access when appropriate.</p>

        <h2>4. Third-party AI providers</h2>
        <p>Conclave AX can use third-party AI services through configured AI Accounts. You are responsible for complying with the terms, acceptable-use requirements, subscription conditions, and usage charges of those providers.</p>

        <h2>5. Work outputs</h2>
        <p>AI-generated code, analysis, reviews, tests, and other outputs may be incomplete or incorrect. You are responsible for reviewing outputs and deciding whether they are appropriate to use, merge, publish, or deploy.</p>

        <h2>6. Public website</h2>
        <p>The public website is provided for product information. Do not submit passwords, API keys, private source code, or other confidential execution material through unauthenticated public-site channels.</p>

        <h2>7. Service changes and availability</h2>
        <p>Conclave AX may change as capabilities are improved, added, or removed. Availability may be interrupted for maintenance, provider outages, security work, or infrastructure changes.</p>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </Section>
</SiteLayout>
